WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.360
Conservatives should care about the 2020
decennial census. For one, it's mandated

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.799
in the US Constitution. And right up top.
Fidelity to the Constitution implies

00:00:13.799 --> 00:00:17.880
fidelity to a fair and accurate census.
In addition, the census is critical to

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.270
American business. The best way for a
free market to work efficiently and

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:24.930
fairly is for businesses of every size
to have access to accurate information

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:29.220
to help them make critical decisions. If
conservatives want businesses to make

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:33.390
the best decisions possible, they should
want a fair and accurate census. A major

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:37.649
threat to the accuracy of the census is
underfunding. Why? Due to rhetoric coming

00:00:37.649 --> 00:00:40.739
from Washington, members of some
immigrant and minority communities have

00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:44.610
already shown concern about answering
census questions. The commerce

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:48.120
secretary's unfortunate decision to
include a citizenship question makes

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:51.690
matters worse. The more reluctant people
are to answer the survey, the more money

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:55.350
census will have to spend to get their
answers. In addition, census is

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:59.280
employing new technologies for the 2020
count that will save taxpayers money in

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:02.730
the long run, but those technologies need
to be tested and protected against

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:07.520
threats. An accurate census is in all our
interests. Congress needs to step up.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:12.140
What do you think about the 2020 census and the citizenship question? Let us know in your

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:15.900
comments. Also, let us know what other
topics you'd like our scholars to cover

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:22.500
in 60 seconds, and be sure to like and
subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

